**Corollary 5.5 (infinite image and sourcewise termination).** If NPL returns an
infinite full-row image, no finite complete field and uniform finite new-read cap
can give exact recovery. If the image is finite but neither generated frame is
admitted for all its rows, this procedure returns OUTSIDE for its alphabet
optimization and leaves unrestricted uniform recovery open. Regardless of
admission, every actual finite original under Assumption 1.3 has a sourcewise
terminating static recovery service: decode its original root, recursively decode
children only after their original parent reports branch, and then compute the
full $Q$-row. There need be no uniform call or word-length bound on that traversal.

Proof. A field with $m$ conditional values and a consumer with at most $K$ reads
has at most $m4^K$ possible full outputs, contradicting infinite image. OUTSIDE
has Definition 3.4's meaning. For traversal, each original node takes at most two
paid current-register reads by the supplied decoder. The finite original has
finitely many nodes; its reconstructed description supports finite local row
computation and an actual halt. No update, reset, clone or old-version access is
used. Unbounded source size can make the sourcewise costs unbounded. $\square$

